{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Or a burn's scar.</b> שנימני\"ט; when the burn healed it turned into a depressed bright spot or a smooth white one. And the signs of a burn and the signs of a boil are the same — so why did Scripture separate them? To teach that they do not combine with each other — if half a gris arose in a boil and half a gris in a burn, they are not assessed as a gris (Ḥullin 8a)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "The lemma includes the Old French la'az 'שנימני\"ט' (Old French senimanti or similar); the exact French identification is uncertain, so it is left in Hebrew script unresolved."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:11.472717582Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}